      "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b",
      "sql": "WITH FilteredOrders AS (\n    SELECT \n        st.Name AS Territory,\n        sod.OrderQty,\n        sod.LineTotal\n    FROM Sales.SalesOrderDetail sod\n    JOIN Sales.SalesOrderHeader soh ON sod.SalesOrderID = soh.SalesOrderID\n    JOIN Sales.SalesTerritory st ON soh.TerritoryID = st.TerritoryID\n    JOIN Production.Product p ON sod.ProductID = p.ProductID\n    JOIN Production.ProductSubcategory psc ON p.ProductSubcategoryID = psc.ProductSubcategoryID\n    WHERE soh.OrderDate >= @start_date\n      AND soh.OrderDate <= @end_date\n      AND st.[Group] = 'Europe'\n      AND psc.Name = 'Road Bikes'\n)\nSELECT \n    Territory,\n    SUM(OrderQty) AS Units,\n    ROUND(SUM(LineTotal), 2) AS Sales\nFROM FilteredOrders\nGROUP BY Territory\nORDER BY Sales DESC;",
      "explanation": "The query follows the SOP exactly: filters orders by date range and European territories, joins to product subcategory to filter for 'Road Bikes', aggregates quantity and line total per territory, rounds sales to 2 decimals, and sorts by sales descending. All table names are schema-qualified. No extra tables needed.",
